component Identity {
  goal {
    Establish who is acting on every page and action, with one account type and
    email and password sign-in, so the rest of Slotted never guesses.
  }

  state {
    Identity owns each *user account*, which has one email and one password
    credential and no stored role.

    Identity owns each *session* created at sign-in and ended at sign-out.
  }

  logic {
    Resolving the *signed-in user* takes four steps. Step one reads the session
    from the request headers. Step two looks up the user account that the session
    belongs to. Step three returns the signed-in user, or returns no user when the
    session is missing or invalid. Step four turns a missing user into an
    unauthenticated refusal at the requireUser gate, and otherwise hands the
    signed-in user to the calling page or action.
  }

  constraints {
    The optimistic redirect on the session cookie is not a security boundary. Only
    requireUser may decide whether a signed-in user exists for a page or action.

    Module commands and queries must not read the session themselves. They take the
    signed-in user as an explicit actor.

    A user account must not carry a role. Owning and renting come from a user's
    relationship to rooms and requests.
  }

  cases {
    Signing up and then signing in creates a session, and resolving the
    signed-in user from that session's headers returns the user.

    Resolving the signed-in user with no session or an invalid one returns no user,
    and requireUser then refuses as unauthenticated.

    Submitting a form after clearing the session changes nothing and is refused.

    Signing out ends the session, and the next page load redirects to sign-in.
  }

  interface {
    Identity lets a person sign up, sign in, and sign out with email and password
    on a user account.

    Identity provides requireUser, which returns the signed-in user for the current
    session or refuses as unauthenticated. Every page and action except sign-up and
    sign-in calls it.

    Identity provides resolution of the session from request headers outside
    Next.js, so the signed-in user can be tested without a running app.
  }

  decisions {
    Better Auth backs Identity because Auth.js is security-fixes-only and Lucia is
    deprecated.

    Roles come from the relationship, not the account, so one person can own and
    rent without two accounts.
  }
}
